  "notes": "Compound of {隔|かく} (to separate/partition) + {離|り} (to detach/distance). Carries a clinical or official tone.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {隔離|かくり}する (to isolate; to quarantine)\n- {隔離|かくり}{期間|きかん} (quarantine period)\n- {隔離|かくり}{施設|しせつ} (quarantine facility)\n- {隔離|かくり}{病棟|びょうとう} (isolation ward)\n- {自宅|じたく}{隔離|かくり} (home quarantine)\n\nUSAGE:\nBecame widely known during the COVID-19 pandemic. Also used historically for the forced segregation of people with diseases such as Hansen's disease (leprosy).",
